  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins200.html",
  "prefLabel": "Ins 205.01 Date of Issuance or Filing of Documents",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ins 205.01 Date of Issuance or Filing of Documents.\n\n(a) All decisions, orders, notices, or other written correspondence or documents issued by or at the direction of the department shall be refutably presumed to have been issued on the date noted on the document.\n\n(b) All written documents governed by these rules shall be deemed to have been filed with or received by the department on the actual date of receipt by the department, as evidenced by a date stamp placed on the document by the department in the normal course of business.\n\n(c) A decision, order, notice, or other written correspondence or document issued by the department shall be deemed to have been received on the day it is:\n\n(1) Delivered to a party or left at the physical address of that person, if delivery is by personal delivery;\n\n(2) Deposited in a depository of the United States Postal Service, if delivery is by first class mail; or\n\n(3) Faxed or sent electronically, if delivery is by electronic mail.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Ins 200) #13073-A, eff 7-27-20",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins200.html"
}
